    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "dumping some thoughts here, auto-tuning single-gpu kernels should be easier to start with. but we should also be aware that sometimes we want to benchmark multi-gpu kernels as well, such as selecting allreduce implementations. autotuning for these algorithms will pose many challenges: we need to make sure every process launches the operation at the same time, with exactly the same order. cc @zou3519 ",
